From be1fab215ea64bc9337af54ee98d21d46b3e6b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:10:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 62/71] Keep the summarization request on the cached prefix

The summarization request was billed at full price for the entire history it
was about to discard. It sent no tools, and an empty tool list is not neutral:
the request then omits the `tools` field altogether, so the prompt ahead of the
conversation changes and the whole history re-prefills. Compaction has no step
of its own, so it now borrows the tool specs of the step the turn last executed
- the same list the surrounding requests sent.

Measured across the eight compactions in `~/.suffice`, every one is 0% cached
at ~73-82K tokens, $0.036 or 4.1% of the bill. The A/B runs that carried this
line on 2026-09-04 came back 83-99% cached.

Tools now sit in front of a model that is only asked to write prose.
`drain_to_completed` records what comes back without dispatching it, so a tool
call would not run, but it would leave the turn with no assistant message and
`get_last_assistant_message_from_turn` would silently fall back to an older
one. The packaged defaults therefore carry the upstream summarization prompt
with one sentence appended, which keeps the prompt template itself untouched.
The prompt is the trailing user message, appended after the whole history, so
the sentence costs a few fresh tokens and touches no prefix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
